---
// Comparison page. Copy authored against briefs/maltipoo-vs-cavapoo.json (2026-07-13).
// HARD RULE: verdicts mirror cavapoopuppy.sg's published comparison exactly.
// Cross-link to cavapoopuppy.sg/cavapoo-vs-maltipoo added at launch (both repos).
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import AnswerCapsule from '../components/AnswerCapsule.astro';
import CaptionedBlock from '../components/CaptionedBlock.astro';
import FactsCard from '../components/FactsCard.astro';
import FAQ from '../components/FAQ.astro';
import CtaClose from '../components/CtaClose.astro';
import { site, whatsappLink } from '../data/site';
import { webPageSchema, breadcrumbSchema, faqSchema } from '../lib/schema';
import featuredImg from '../assets/site/21-maltipoo-vs-cavapoo.webp';

const title = 'Maltipoo vs Cavapoo: Which Fits Your Home | Maltipoo.sg';
const description =
  'Maltipoo vs Cavapoo for Singapore homes: the honest split. Maltipoos want daytime company; Cavapoos handle working households. Size, coat, price and the routine test.';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Compare Breeds', url: '/compare-maltipoo' },
  { name: 'Maltipoo vs Cavapoo', url: '/maltipoo-vs-cavapoo' },
];

const faqItems = [
  {
    q: 'Which barks more, a Maltipoo or a Cavapoo?',
    a: 'The Maltipoo, honestly. It inherits the Maltese alert streak and gets louder when lonely. A Cavapoo is quieter on average and more forgiving of an empty flat. With daytime company and early quiet training, a Maltipoo stays neighbour-friendly.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which is calmer?',
    a: 'It depends when you look. A Cavapoo is more even-keeled when alone. A Maltipoo with company is one of the calmest lap dogs there is; a Maltipoo without company is not. That single sentence is most of this comparison.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What about a Cockapoo as a third option?',
    a: 'Whether you searched cavapoo vs maltipoo vs cockapoo or the reverse, the triangle is simple: a Cockapoo is the sportier, usually larger cousin of the pair, better for households that want longer walks. It suits active homes rather than lap-dog homes; the cockapoo comparison covers it properly.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is there a price difference between Maltipoo and Cavapoo?',
    a: 'Not at our shops: both run $3,288 to $5,988 all-in with the same starter kit, delivery, training lesson and licensing included. Which removes the last excuse to choose on anything except fit.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Are both HDB approved?',
    a: 'Yes, both by the same rule. HDB’s list approves a cross of any two approved breeds (item 62); the Maltese, Toy Poodle and Cavalier King Charles Spaniel are all named on the list.',
  },
];

const schemas = [
  webPageSchema({
    path: '/maltipoo-vs-cavapoo',
    title,
    description,
    aboutName: 'Maltipoo vs Cavapoo comparison',
    datePublished: '2026-07-13',
  }),
  breadcrumbSchema(crumbs),
  faqSchema(faqItems),
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/maltipoo-vs-cavapoo" schemas={schemas}>
  <section class="container-site pt-4">
    <div class="rounded-[var(--radius-panel)] bg-tint-200 px-6 py-10 md:px-12">
      <Breadcrumb items={crumbs} bare class="mb-5" />
      <p class="eyebrow mb-2">Comparison</p>
      <h1 class="text-[clamp(1.9rem,4vw,2.8rem)] mb-3 max-w-[24ch]">Maltipoo vs Cavapoo for Singapore homes</h1>
      <p class="text-ink-soft max-w-[52ch] mb-5">
        Our parent business places both breeds, so we have no reason to spin this one. The
        difference is real, and it is about your calendar, not the dogs.
      </p>
      <a href={whatsappLink('Hi! Could you help me decide between a Maltipoo and a Cavapoo for my routine?')} class="btn-cta">Ask which fits you</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <AnswerCapsule question="Maltipoo or Cavapoo: which should you choose?">
    Choose a Maltipoo if someone is home most of the day: it is smaller (2 to 4kg), more
    affectionate, and more attachment-dependent. Choose a Cavapoo if the household is out
    working: it is more independent, slightly larger, and settles alone better. Both are
    low-shedding, HDB-approved crosses at {site.pricing.range} all-in here, so fit decides,
    not price.
  </AnswerCapsule>

  <section class="container-site pt-8">
    <img
      src={featuredImg.src}
      width={featuredImg.width}
      height={featuredImg.height}
      alt="Apricot Maltipoo beside a blenheim Cavapoo on a sofa"
      loading="lazy"
      class="rounded-[var(--radius-media)] w-full h-auto shadow-[var(--shadow-pop)]"
    />
  </section>

  <CaptionedBlock heading="Same family, different wiring" id="wiring">
    <p>
      Both are Poodle crosses with quick minds and low-shedding coats, and the difference
      between Maltipoo and Cavapoo sits in the other parent. The Maltese brings devotion with
      an alert, vocal streak: a dog that wants to be ON you and says so. The Cavalier brings
      an easygoing, portable calm that tolerates an empty flat far better.
    </p>
    <p>
      The "which is better maltipoo or cavapoo" question has no universal answer, only a routine answer: neither wiring is better; each is better FOR someone. The
      <a href="/maltipoo-temperament">Maltipoo temperament guide</a> describes the velcro
      version in full, including the barking honesty most comparisons skip.
    </p>
    <FactsCard
      slot="side"
      heading="The wiring in one card"
      items={[
        'Maltipoo: devoted, vocal, wants daytime company',
        'Cavapoo: easygoing, quieter, more independent',
        'Both: clever, low-shedding, flat-sized',
      ]}
    />
  </CaptionedBlock>

  <CaptionedBlock heading="Size, coat and colours, side by side" id="specs" reverse>
    <p>
      The maltipoo vs cavapoo size gap is small but real: our toy Maltipoos finish 2 to 4kg,
      toy Cavapoos more like 3 to 5kg with minis larger, per the
      <a href="/maltipoo-size">size guide</a>. Coats on both run wavy to curly and
      low-shedding; colours diverge, with Maltipoos here overwhelmingly apricot and Cavapoos
      spanning blenheim, ruby, apricot and black.
    </p>
    <FactsCard
      slot="side"
      heading="Specs, kg-first"
      items={[
        'Maltipoo toy: 2 to 4kg full grown',
        'Cavapoo toy: 3 to 5kg, minis to 10kg',
        'Coats: both wavy-to-curly, low-shedding',
        'Colours: apricot vs blenheim/ruby spectrum',
        'HDB: both approved by rule 62',
      ]}
    />
  </CaptionedBlock>

  <CaptionedBlock heading="Price: identical here, so fit decides" id="price" tinted>
    <p>
      At our shops the cavapoo vs maltipoo price question has a boring answer: both breeds run
      the same {site.pricing.range} all-in, same starter kit, same delivery and setup, same
      trainer lesson, same licensing at purchase. The
      <a href="/maltipoo-price-singapore">price guide</a> breaks the range down.
    </p>
    <p>
      We publish that on purpose. When price cannot break the tie, the only question left is
      the right one: who is home between 8am and 6pm?
    </p>
    <FactsCard
      slot="side"
      heading="The decision, reduced"
      items={[
        'Price: identical range, both breeds',
        'HDB: identical, both approved',
        'Coat care: near-identical',
        'Remaining variable: your daytime routine',
      ]}
    />
  </CaptionedBlock>

  <CaptionedBlock heading="The mismatch we keep seeing" id="mismatch">
    <p>
      The single most common mismatch in our placement history: a couple out from 8am to 6pm,
      set on a Maltipoo because of the face. Maltipoos want far more daytime company, so we
      explain the wiring and point them to a Cavapoo, and the sale walks across to our sister
      shop instead of into a bad year.
    </p>
    <p>
      It runs the other way too: retirees offered a Cavapoo elsewhere when what they wanted
      was a shadow on the sofa all day, which is Maltipoo work. Our sister site's
      <a href="https://cavapoopuppy.sg/cavapoo-vs-maltipoo" rel="noopener">Cavapoo side of this comparison</a>
      tells the same story from the other sofa. Tell us your routine on
      WhatsApp ({site.phoneDisplay}) and you will get the honest routing, whichever direction
      it points.
    </p>
    <FactsCard
      slot="side"
      heading="Honest routing"
      items={[
        'Empty weekday flat: Cavapoo, at our sister shop',
        'Someone home most days: Maltipoo, here',
        'Either way: same parent business, same aftercare',
      ]}
    />
  </CaptionedBlock>

  <FAQ items={faqItems} />

  <CtaClose
    secondaryHeading="Compare more breeds"
    secondaryText="Maltese, Toy Poodle, Bichon, Shih Tzu and Cockapoo, all against the Maltipoo."
    secondaryHref="/compare-maltipoo"
    secondaryLabel="See all comparisons"
  />
</BaseLayout>
